WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.120 --> 00:02.620
In one of the longest-running studies in history,

2
00:02.680 --> 00:08.300
researchers found that the biggest predictor of health,
happiness and longevity amongst the participants

3
00:08.360 --> 00:10.620
was strong social connections.

4
00:10.680 --> 00:19.500
What this means for us is that our ability to cultivate strong relationships
plays an important role in our learning, well-being and resilience.

5
00:19.560 --> 00:24.540
There are four not-so-secret secrets
to establishing strong relationships:

6
00:24.760 --> 00:29.580
attention, vulnerability, empathy, and compassion.

7
00:30.040 --> 00:34.860
AVEC, which means “with” in French, is an appropriate coincidence,

8
00:34.920 --> 00:40.060
since interpersonal resilience is all about
how we interact with others.

9
00:40.226 --> 00:44.246
With attention, we tune into other people and get curious.

10
00:44.306 --> 00:49.926
Making eye contact activates our social brain,
our parasympathetic nervous system.

11
00:49.986 --> 00:54.806
So we physically turn our body towards the person
and maintain eye contact.

12
00:54.866 --> 01:00.086
We listen actively, ask genuine questions,
and withhold judgment.

13
01:02.786 --> 01:07.046
With vulnerability, we express ourselves fully and authentically.

14
01:07.186 --> 01:10.406
While it may feel like we are stepping out of our comfort zone,

15
01:10.466 --> 01:16.566
sharing our thoughts and emotions and accepting responsibility,
even in the toughest situations,

16
01:16.626 --> 01:19.526
has a positive impact on our relationships.

17
01:19.666 --> 01:25.118
There's also power in acknowledging our fears,
or simply saying, “I don't know.”

18
01:25.338 --> 01:32.638
With empathy, we try to understand and identify with the emotions
and perspectives that others bring to the situation.

19
01:32.858 --> 01:37.038
We listen deeply in order to understand
what they're going through.

20
01:37.098 --> 01:40.398
Empathy is the foundation for compassion.

21
01:42.378 --> 01:49.118
And with compassion, we demonstrate our concern for others
and our desire to alleviate their pain.

22
01:49.178 --> 01:54.718
We communicate that we genuinely want to be of service
by offering help and support.

23
01:54.778 --> 01:59.518
Together, these four elements help us form
those important social connections.

24
01:59.578 --> 02:09.178
Without them, we miss the opportunity to build the strong relationships
necessary to do our best individual and collective work.
